{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And thus shall you do to them, to cleanse them: sprinkle upon them water of sin-offering.</b> Water of the ashes of the red heifer. And this was because of those among them who were impure from the dead, for they had slain those who made the calf, as it says (Exodus 32:27): ״והרגו איש את אחיו ואיש את רעהו״." "<b>And they shall pass a razor over all their flesh.</b> Even the beard, even the side-locks — he required of them a complete shaving like the metzora, about whom it is written (Leviticus 14:9): ״יגלח את כל שערו את ראשו ואת זקנו ואת גבות עיניו״ — because the Levites were the substitutes for the firstborn who were disqualified through the calf, and idolatry is called זבחי מתים — sacrifices to the dead, and a metzora is considered like a dead person. And had they not been cleansed by means of this procedure that is mentioned in the parashah, it would not have been possible for them to enter into the service, as it is written at the end: ״ואחרי כן יבאו הלוים לעבוד את עבודת אהל מועד״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:47.482690369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}